# Caparocti Sunborn attacks on turn 3 and its trigger asks whether to tap two untapped artifacts and/or creatures. Bot1 has
# three Ornithopters, two of which came in this turn: a permanent that came under your control this turn can be tapped for a
# cost that is not a {T} symbol (CR 302.6, 118.3), so Bot1 chooses one old and one new, leaving the third untapped. Caparocti
# itself is tapped (attacking) and can't be chosen. Then discover 3 (CR 701.57a): Hero of Bladehold (mana value 4) is exiled and
# passed over (discover 4 would cast it), Fiery Temper (mana value 3, so discover 2 would pass it too) is cast for free at
# Bot2 (3 damage), and the Hero goes to the bottom. Caparocti deals its 4 unblocked: Bot2 20 - 3 - 4 = 13.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Caparocti Sunborn
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Hero of Bladehold
Fiery Temper
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Caparocti Sunborn.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Attack(Caparocti Sunborn > Bot2)
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter#1; Ornithopter#2)
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Tapped = true
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Stack.Count = 0
Exile.Count = 0
Bot2.Life = 13
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Caparocti Sunborn.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#3.Tapped = false
Bot1.Graveyard = Fiery Temper
Bot1.Hand.Count = 0
Bot1.Library.Count = 11
Bot1.Library = Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Hero of Bladehold
